,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Sikkim - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Sikkim,"Music of Sikkim ranges from traditional Nepali folk music to Westernized pop music. The ethnic communities, Lepcha, Limbu, Bhutia, Kiratis and Nepalis constitute the music which is an ingrained part of Sikkimese culture.",Sikkimese,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Sikkim — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Music_of_Sikkim,"Rooted in oral storytelling practices passed down through generations, Sikkimese music serves as a vital expression of cultural identity, blending ancient communal songs with modern adaptations influenced by globalization and migration.",Sikkimese,Sino-Tibetan
2,Sikkimese Bhutia song collection by Denzong Lughar Sungkyop ...Sikkimese Bhutia Song - YouTube MusicFolk Music of Sikkim: A Cultural Tapestry - Orchids IntlTHE ENDLESS NOTE: FOLK INSTRUMENTS OF SIKKIMRHYTHMS OF THE HILLS: THE IMPORTANCE OF VARIOUS MUSICAL ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k5QsmvUOzLM,"Apr 15, 2025 · We have recreated the traditional Sikkimese Bhutia folk song with a modern twist, blending its soulful melodies with contemporary elements to give it a fresh and unique vibe. Listen to Sikkimese Bhutia Song on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more. Sep 16, 2024 · Their cultures constitute the folk dances and music of the Sikkimese area. Their music and folk dances depict the beauty of the natural habitat, illustrate the harvest season, and are performed for good luck and prosperity. Nov 18, 2022 · The documentary is successful in establishing the omnipresence of folk music in our everyday lives—be it celebrations, festivals, death, birth, rituals to the ordinary humdrum of life, folk music always finds a way into our lives. This article explores the significance of various musical instruments in Sikkimese folk music, highlighting how they contribute to storytelling, ritual practices, and communal gatherings.",Sikkimese,Sino-Tibetan
